        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Valerie Daggett, Michael Levitt, Irwin Kuntz, Peter Kollman\n- Organizations: University of Washington, University of California, San Francisco, Stanford University\n- Places: Seattle, Washington, United States\n- Roles: professor of bioengineering, professor of structural biology, postdoctoral researcher, Ph.D. advisor\n- Topics: bioengineering, structural biology, biophysics, Nobel Prize in Chemistry\n\nFacts:\n- Michael Levitt was born on 9 May 1947.\n- Michael Levitt is an American-British-Israeli biophysicist.\n- Since 1987, Michael Levitt has been a professor of structural biology at Stanford University.\n- Valerie Daggett received her Ph.D. from the University of California, San Francisco, where Irwin Kuntz and Peter Kollman advised her.\n- Valerie Daggett subsequently held a postdoctoral position at Stanford University with Michael Levitt.\n- Michael Levitt was a co-recipient of the 2013 Nobel Prize in Chemistry.\n- Valerie Daggett is a professor of bioengineering at the University of Washington in Seattle, Washington, United States.",
